<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pithana</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">18th century BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pithana was a king of Kussara in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> in the 18th century BCE. According to the inscription of his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anitta">Anitta</a>, he captured the trading city of Nesa (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kanesh">Kanesh</a>) by night and treated its people well. Pithana and Anitta built the first large state of central Anatolia, a forerunner of the Hittite kingdom.</p></div>
